# Publish completed work

When a user-requested change in this repository is complete, run the relevant checks, review the diff, then commit only the files changed for that task and push the commit to `origin`. Do this as part of the task without waiting for a separate request to publish.

Push the current branch to the branch of the same name. For work on `main`, push to `origin/main`. Never force-push or overwrite remote history. Before pushing, fetch and confirm the remote branch has not advanced; if it has, integrate the remote changes safely before pushing.

Do not include pre-existing or unrelated changes in the commit. If authentication, checks, conflicts, or repository rules prevent publication, preserve the work and clearly report what remains to be done. Never publish an incomplete change just because a file was saved.
